142
00:10:22,867 --> 00:10:25,806
Can you show me a persistent database?

143
00:10:26,367 --> 00:10:30,413
A database in a container is only as durable as its storage.

144
00:10:30,413 --> 00:10:34,998
With a named volume at the right path, you can remove the container,

145
00:10:34,998 --> 00:10:41,472
upgrade the image within the same major version, or move to a new container, and the data stays.

146
00:10:41,472 --> 00:10:49,901
With the wrong path, the database writes into the container (or into an anonymous volume) and the next redeploy starts empty.

